          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "so that things look a bit nicer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 12.84,
          "en": "And therefore attached you find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.84,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "an updated main-header.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "which you should use to replace your file with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 23.64,
          "en": "So replace the content in your main-header.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.64,
          "end": 27.963,
          "en": "with the content of the attached main-header.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "It's still a very simple file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "but it now got a slightly different markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "and some extra IDs and so on to improve the styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "so that with the file you should have a header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 42.18,
          "en": "that looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 44.16,
          "en": "It's still not perfect though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.16,
          "end": 48.87,
          "en": "Instead, what you should also do to improve the styling here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 53.87,
          "en": "is go to the layout.js file and wrap the MainHeader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.837,
          "end": 57.723,
          "en": "and the children content here with a div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 62.373,
          "en": "and give that div an id of page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 67.29,
          "en": "This again, is only done for styling purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.29,
          "end": 70.5,
          "en": "And with that we now got some padding here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.5,
          "end": 72.123,
          "en": "and this looks nicer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.99,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "With that, if you go to the News Page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 77.34,
          "en": "this also already looks a bit nicer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "but of course these links don't look that great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 86.21000000000001,
          "en": "To make them look better, we can go to the news page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "where we have all these links,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "and in there on that unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "add a class with the className prop of news-list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.56,
          "end": 100.38,
          "en": "which is also one of the classes I'm targeting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.38,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "in that globals.css file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "which was part of the starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 109.35,
          "en": "and save that updated page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.35,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "With that, those news items definitely look different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 115.89,
          "en": "maybe not great yet but that will change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.89,
          "end": 119.16,
          "en": "once we start adding some images to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 124.16,
          "en": "And to add some images to them, we need some dummy data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 125.82,
          "en": "Now in the starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.82,
          "end": 129.48,
          "en": "I actually did already add some dummy images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.48,
          "end": 130.71,
          "en": "in the public folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.71,
          "end": 134.28,
          "en": "There you have a images sub-folder with a news sub-folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.28,
          "end": 136.38,
          "en": "which includes some dummy images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.38,
          "end": 138.303,
          "en": "which we'll use for this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "However, the general news data is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 147.32999999999998,
          "en": "and therefore attached, you also find a dummy-news.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.32999999999998,
          "end": 148.95,
          "en": "which you should copy and paste",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.95,
          "end": 151.98,
          "en": "right into your route project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.98,
          "end": 155.913,
          "en": "so that it sits next to the app and components folders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "And in there you see I'm exporting an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 163.53,
          "en": "with some DUMMY_NEWS data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "where every news item has an id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 169.92000000000002,
          "en": "a slug, which is essentially also an id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.92000000000002,
          "end": 173.01,
          "en": "just in a more search engine-friendly way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "and a bit more readable than an id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 180.33,
          "en": "And then a title image, a date, and some dummy content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.33,
          "end": 183.873,
          "en": "And that's the dummy data we'll use throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "So with that dummy-news.js file added back on the News Page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "you should add a import at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 196.86,
          "en": "and import the DUMMY_NEWS from that dummy-news.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.86,
          "end": 199.47,
          "en": "in the root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.47,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "And instead of outputting the links like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 204.37,
          "en": "we can now use the DUMMY_NEWS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.62,
          "end": 209.14,
          "en": "to map them into JSX elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.15,
          "end": 213.18,
          "en": "by taking the individual newsItems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 216.72,
          "en": "and for every newsItem, I wanna output a list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.72,
          "end": 221.72,
          "en": "with a key of newsItem.id, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 227.21,
          "en": "And then inside of that list item, I wanna have a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 230.853,
          "en": "because these news items should still be clickable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.96,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "And the ref of that link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 238.02,
          "en": "should now be dynamically constructed string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.02,
          "end": 243.02,
          "en": "using that template string feature JavaScript offers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 245.6,
          "en": "where we point at /news/",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.48,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "and then some dynamically injected value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "which is different for every news item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 254.49,
          "en": "And that could now either be the id or the slug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.49,
          "end": 257.07,
          "en": "Both is unique, and I'll use the slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.07,
          "end": 260.553,
          "en": "since that gives us nicer looking URLs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.53,
          "en": "So with that, we got clickable links here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.53,
          "end": 267.3,
          "en": "clickable newsItems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 267.3,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "and the content for every newsItem should now be an image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 276.77,
          "en": "where the source is also a dynamically constructed string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.78,
          "end": 281.163,
          "en": "where we load an image from /images/news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.27,
          "end": 284.64,
          "en": "because that's that folder structure we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 284.64,
          "end": 285.93,
          "en": "in the public folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 285.93,
          "end": 289.53,
          "en": "We have a images folder there and then a nested news folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 289.53,
          "end": 291.663,
          "en": "which contains the newsImages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.15999999999997,
          "end": 295.59000000000003,
          "en": "Well and then the image names are stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 295.59000000000003,
          "end": 298.443,
          "en": "in the dummy news items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 299.58,
          "end": 302.55,
          "en": "So they offer in page.js, it's now /",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 302.55,
          "end": 305.55,
          "en": "and then again some dynamically injected value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 305.55,
          "end": 309.39300000000003,
          "en": "where we point at newsItem.image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.1,
          "end": 314.4,
          "en": "And then we can also give those images an alt text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 314.4,
          "end": 318.423,
          "en": "where I will simply use the title of my news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 319.8,
          "end": 322.17,
          "en": "And below that image in that link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.17,
          "end": 324.3,
          "en": "I'd now like to have a span",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 324.3,
          "end": 328.113,
          "en": "where we simply output the newsItem.title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.39,
          "end": 334.29,
          "en": "With that, if you save this now and you go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 334.29,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "you'll have a nicer News Page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 338.64,
          "en": "where we can see those different news items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 338.64,
          "end": 341.13,
          "en": "which are these clickable boxes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 341.13,
          "end": 342.63,
          "en": "And when we click one of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.63,
          "end": 344.82,
          "en": "we're taken to the News Detail Page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 344.82,
          "end": 348.213,
          "en": "And of course, that page can now also be improved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 349.11,
          "end": 352.44,
          "en": "Here in that News Detail Page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 352.44,
          "end": 355.08,
          "en": "I'd like to output something different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.08,
          "end": 357.573,
          "en": "than this dummy text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 358.40999999999997,
          "end": 362.85,
          "en": "and therefore I'll start by identifying the actual newsItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 362.85,
          "end": 364.983,
          "en": "for which we're showing the details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 365.94,
          "end": 368.01,
          "en": "For that we can again use the DUMMY_NEWS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 368.01,
          "end": 371.433,
          "en": "which therefore must be imported into this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 372.27,
          "end": 376.08,
          "en": "And then we can use the find method to find a newsItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 376.08,
          "end": 380.76,
          "en": "by taking a look at the slug of that newsItem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 380.76,
          "end": 382.56,
          "en": "And we have to take a look at the slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 382.56,
          "end": 384.18,
          "en": "because in the news page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 384.18,
          "end": 387.96,
          "en": "we're actually using the slug in the link path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 387.96,
          "end": 390.813,
          "en": "so that slug will be encoded in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 392.37,
          "end": 395.90999999999997,
          "en": "And hence we might want to name this here newsSlug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 395.90999999999997,
          "end": 398.73,
          "en": "because it's actually the slug we're extracting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 398.73,
          "end": 399.563,
          "en": "from the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 401.49,
          "end": 405.96,
          "en": "We could also rename our placeholder from id to slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 405.96,
          "end": 409.86,
          "en": "to make that clear, and I'll do that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 409.86,
          "end": 411.84000000000003,
          "en": "Of course, changing that name means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 411.84000000000003,
          "end": 414.9,
          "en": "that we also have to access params.slug now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 414.9,
          "end": 416.733,
          "en": "instead of params.id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 417.72,
          "end": 420.27,
          "en": "But now we can compare the slug of one of the newsItems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 420.27,
          "end": 424.77,
          "en": "from the DUMMY_NEWS array to this newsSlug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 424.77,
          "end": 427.74,
          "en": "and it's the item where both are equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 427.74,
          "end": 430.503,
          "en": "which we wanna show on this detail page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 432,
          "end": 436.65,
          "en": "So with that here, we could then replace this fragment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 436.65,
          "end": 439.2,
          "en": "with the article element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 439.2,
          "end": 444.2,
          "en": "and then output the actual title of the newsItem we found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 445.08,
          "end": 448.803,
          "en": "and maybe wrap this in a header element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 449.97,
          "end": 453.69,
          "en": "And then above this h1 element, I wanna output the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
